WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.328 --> 00:00:02.826
- What's the number one thing
you want everyone in this room

00:00:02.826 --> 00:00:03.914
to walk away with?

00:00:03.914 --> 00:00:07.215
- That I think there's literally
300 million different ways to

00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:10.916
win in the US if that's how
many people we have. Right?

00:00:10.916 --> 00:00:14.983
There is no blueprint,
there is no exact way.

00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:18.312
It only comes down to being
able to factor in the 40 or 50

00:00:18.312 --> 00:00:22.039
indexes, input points,
context points around your life.

00:00:22.039 --> 00:00:25.308
And then
navigating through that.

00:00:25.308 --> 00:00:28.163
What I really want is for people
to understand don't do it

00:00:28.163 --> 00:00:30.172
like me, don't would like you,
don't do it like Zucks,

00:00:30.172 --> 00:00:32.330
don't do it like Travis,
don't do like Cuban.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.453
Spend as much time as you can,

00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:36.579
Steph, I'll be honest 
with you maybe you

00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:39.151
know the answer, I'm actually
weirdly asking you if I knew how

00:00:39.151 --> 00:00:42.727
to help people create 
more self-awareness,

00:00:42.727 --> 00:00:44.384
it's what I would sell.

00:00:44.384 --> 00:00:46.643
I don't know if that becomes
through therapy or some system

00:00:46.643 --> 00:00:48.268
I don't know, I really don't.

00:00:48.268 --> 00:00:51.420
- [Stephanie] My fear is 
actually the reverse in terms

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.314
of with all the information, 
with all the self-help,

00:00:55.314 --> 00:00:57.039
with all the people on and 
Instagram saying

00:00:57.039 --> 00:00:58.854
these three easy steps.

00:00:58.854 --> 00:01:02.927
The fear is we are telling
people as soon as you have a job

00:01:02.927 --> 00:01:05.736
if you have a job like, click,
and when you meet a man that you

00:01:05.736 --> 00:01:07.740
like, click, and then you can
afford a house and you have a

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.216
baby all of these things
are the recipe for success.

00:01:11.216 --> 00:01:14.815
Well, if you're using some
kind of Cosmo checklist for the

00:01:14.815 --> 00:01:18.906
recipe for success you are going
to end up very unhappy because

00:01:18.906 --> 00:01:20.448
success is internal.

00:01:20.448 --> 00:01:21.845
- So I'll go different way.

00:01:21.845 --> 00:01:22.724
Fine.

00:01:22.724 --> 00:01:24.655
But I actually think were in a
much better place than we've

00:01:24.655 --> 00:01:26.474
been in the past 60
years on this issue.

00:01:26.474 --> 00:01:27.157
- Why?

00:01:27.157 --> 00:01:31.276
- Prior to this world where we
had so many more opinions and

00:01:31.276 --> 00:01:35.081
platforms, we had three channels
that told everybody that thing.

00:01:35.081 --> 00:01:38.617
There was three old white guys
that owned ABC and NBC and CBS.

00:01:38.617 --> 00:01:39.730
- [Stephanie] That's a 
great point.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.555
- That completely pushed down to
them what it was supposed to be.

00:01:42.555 --> 00:01:44.532
Now at least we have 
a lot more voices and

00:01:44.532 --> 00:01:46.095
there's more things to navigate.

00:01:46.095 --> 00:01:47.845
(light hip hop music)

